        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kabul</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1500 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The origin of Kabul, who built it and when, is largely unknown; the city is believed to be over 3,500 years old, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rigveda">Rigveda</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avesta">Avesta</a> refer to a settlement called Kubha.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">At an altitude of 1,791 metres in a narrow valley of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-kush">Hindu Kush</a>, on the Kabul River, in the eastern half of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A city of the Achaemenid, Mauryan, Kushan and Mughal worlds; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a>'s headquarters and burial place; the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani Empire</a> from 1776; the Anglo-Afghan wars; the gardens and palaces of Bagh-e Babur and Darul Aman; the wars from 1978 to 2001</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Kabul is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>.</span></div>
